{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":311205,"duration_api_ms":311145,"num_turns":35,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"40473b3f-c07b-46d7-a77f-0ec9d656f79c","total_cost_usd":1.55891125,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":81891,"cache_read_input_tokens":1365585,"output_tokens":14568,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":81891,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":14568,"cacheReadInputTokens":1365585,"cacheCreationInputTokens":81891,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.55891125,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `SubstrateLayerState::default()` (substrate.rs:56), `colonizable_area_cm2` is hardcoded to `100.0`, but the derived value for default geometry (40×25cm, InertSand, 3cm depth) is `1500.0` — a 15× discrepancy. While `refresh_habitat_registry()` always overwrites this, any code that constructs substrate layers via `..Default::default()` and reads `colonizable_area_cm2` before engine initialization will silently get a wrong value. Fix: compute the default via `Self::derived_colonizable_area_cm2` using `TankGeometry::default().footprint_area_cm2()`, or replace the field default with `0.0` and document it as derived-only to make stale reads immediately obvious.","rationale":"The current default creates a silent correctness trap for downstream beads that may construct substrate layers outside the normal `TankState::new()` path. The field is a cached derived value, so a self-consistent or clearly-sentinel default (like 0.0) would prevent latent misuse without any behavioral change to existing code paths."}],"summary":"Thorough review of the habitat registry implementation (habitat.rs, state.rs, substrate.rs, geometry.rs, engine.rs, actions.rs, invariants.rs, save.rs, snapshot.rs, and 780-line test file). All 30 habitat tests pass. The implementation is correct and well-integrated: HabitatKind/HabitatEntry types are properly serialized, colonizable areas are derived from geometry/hardware/plant state (not hardcoded), all three exposure modifiers (flow, oxygen, light) are bounded in [0,1] via both computation-time clamping and invariant enforcement, and the registry is refreshed at every relevant lifecycle point (construction, save/load, daily update, player actions via `affects_habitat_registry()`). The only issue found is a misleading hardcoded default for `SubstrateLayerState::colonizable_area_cm2` that creates a potential future correctness trap. No bugs, safety problems, or significant maintainability risks identified."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"3a5d7731-f560-4681-9d6b-8a9b7718c509"}
